  "notes": "Gan Chinese romanised input contract: the Nanchang-based romanisation used by the Gan Wikipedia, grounded in Ding 2006's Nanchang dialect description. iu spells the front-rounded vowel /y/ as a single nucleus (test 2). Tone is lexical (7 Nanchang citation tones) and not yet encoded; the stress schema does not apply, tonal-language exemption per quality_tiers.md. No WikiPron gold exists in this romanisation (WikiPron's gan_hani file is Han-character keyed), so the tier stays at skeleton.",
